From: djsaunde <1245942+djsaunde@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:31:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] fast: widescreen mapping, a rectangle hook and vertex
 replacements for ports

Three opt-in hooks for a port's rendering enhancements (the 1080 port's widescreen and high-fps
interpolation). Nothing changes until a port turns them on.

gfx_set_widescreen(true): the game view is wider than the native 4:3 and the picture is centred in it
(AdjXForAspectRatio). Partial viewports keep their centre where the picture has it (their width is the
full view's, the vertices inside are narrowed back), partial scissors take the picture's edges, depth
read-back coordinates follow the same mapping, and a persistent colour image (patch 17) is loaded into
the centred 4:3 only, the sides cleared to black (a 2D screen would show a wide 3D frame's leftovers
there). Full-width scissors and viewports still cover the whole view.

gfx_set_rect_hook(hook): called for every G_TEXRECT / G_TEXRECTFLIP / G_FILLRECT with the command and its
U10.2 corners, which the port may move (also beyond the native screen: anchoring a HUD to the view's
edges, lerping a sprite between two frames); *stretch draws it over the view's full width.

gfx_set_vertex_replacements(map): a G_VTX whose source address is a key loads the mapped vertices instead,
the vertex counterpart of Run()'s matrix replacements.
